  "headline": "Government Sets Deadline For 2027 Minimum Wage Determination",
  "seoTitle": "2027 Indonesia Minimum Wage Deadline Announced",
  "metaDescription": "Indonesian authorities mandate the announcement of 2027 provincial minimum wages by November 21, incorporating new calculation formulas.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The Minister of Manpower has instructed regional heads to finalize provincial minimum wage announcements by November 21, 2026.",
    "New wage calculation guidelines incorporate data on the Decent Living Needs (KHL) alongside broader economic indicators.",
    "Labor unions in Yogyakarta have publicly advocated for prioritizing KHL survey results as a primary factor in setting local wage standards."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian government has established a clear timeline for the determination of 2027 minimum wages, requiring provincial-level announcements to be completed no later than November 21, 2026, followed by district-level decisions by November 25. Minister of Manpower Yassierli has officially distributed new calculation guidelines to regional governors, emphasizing that the revised formulas will integrate Kebutuhan Hidup Layak (KHL) or Decent Living Needs data, alongside prevailing economic conditions and existing labor protection regulations. This move comes as the Ministry of Home Affairs, led by Tito Karnavian, urged regional administrations to ensure transparency and stability throughout the process to avoid potential labor disputes. In response, labor organizations are actively lobbying for the inclusion of KHL metrics to ensure that the new wage standards accurately reflect the cost of living and provide adequate support for workers across different provinces.",
